{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLfu6FGhG3WRbkyv6nMq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the plan to `.ard/224/plan.md` and the role file to `.ard/224/triage-engineer.md`, with status done, size L and risk medium. I did not run any build or tests, since this was planning only.\n\n- **Executor:** a scanner job can ask for the repository's history, and Docker mounts the controller's bare clone read-only at `/history`.\n- **Marker file:** a scanner asks for history with an empty `history` file in its role directory. There is no config key, so a config override can't grant another scanner that access.\n- **New scanner:** `internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog-history` is a copy of the HEAD scanner switched to `trufflehog git`. It uses the same fingerprint salt and the same fail-closed checks. It keeps only the detector, file and line, so no secret or commit data leaves the script.\n- **Defaults:** no autoclose, weekly, own timeout, route to needs-human.\n- **Tests:** the plan covers validation, the Docker argv, a Docker integration case, role loading, and no-leak and fail-closed script tests.\n\nOpen points for a maintainer, also in the role file:\n- **Bare-clone mount vs `git bundle`:** please confirm the mount before the worker starts. It exposes every fetched ref, including unmerged PR branches.\n- **Same finding across both scanners:** the fingerprint matches, but each scanner keeps its own snapshot. I didn't check whether the engine turns a value found by both into one issue.\n- **Enabling it in this repo:** that needs a copy under `.ard/scanners/` and an entry in `.ard/config.yaml`. Agents can't edit those, so a maintainer has to.\n- **Kubernetes:** no k8s executor exists yet, so the plan only adds a comment on the contract it will have to meet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3936,